reated-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-63128073-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>63128073</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7331092-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7331092</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9324046-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9324046</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1022314A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO KOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, KOYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, TORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, TORU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO KOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, KOYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A polyamide resin composition which is obtained by melt-kneading (A) a polyamide resin, (B) a phyllosilicate, and (C) either an olefin compound having a carboxylic acid anhydride group in the molecule or a polymer of the olefin compound, wherein the phyllosilicate (B) is one in which exchangeable metal ions present between layers thereof have undergone ion exchange with an organic onium salt and which has reactive functional groups bonded thereto. The composition combines high rigidity with stretchability even when it has a low ash content. It may optionally contain an inorganic filler other than the phyllosilicate, an impact modifier, and a flame retardant. In this case also, the composition retains rigidity and stretchability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de résine de polyamide produite par malaxage à chaud (A) d'une résine de polyamide, (B) d'un phyllosilicate et (C), soit d'une composé oléfinique possédant un groupe anhydride d'acide carboxylique dans la molécule, soit d'un polymère du composé oléfinique. Le phyllosilicate (B) est une structure dans laquelle les ions métal échangeables présents entre les couches de celles-ci ont été soumis à un échange d'ions avec un sel d'onium organique et possède des groupes fonctionnels réactifs liés à celui-ci. La composition combine une rigidité élevée et une étirabilité élevée même lorsque sa teneur en cendres est faible. Elle peut éventuellement contenir une charge inorganique autre que le phyllosilicate, un antichoc et une charge ignifugeante. Dans ce cas également, la composition conserve sa rigidité et son étirabilité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>